  "notes": "Source: official UCF Barry S. Miller College of Business Business Economics BSBA degree page, 'Curricular Plan of Study', transcribed course by course 2026-09-30 from https://business.ucf.edu/degree/economics-business/ (Department of Economics, Orlando FL). Program name per source: Business Economics BSBA. Course titles use the page's wording. CAVEAT (staleness): the page carries no catalog-year label (it defers to the UCF Catalog for the most up-to-date listing); 2026-2027 is used as the page content is the college's current published plan (same convention as the sibling UCF COB plans). (1) Junior Fall header reads '(56 hours)' — an obvious typo; the term lists five standard courses (QMB 3200, MAR 3023, FIN 3403, ACG 3173, GEB 3006), and the sibling accounting page places the identical five-course set (with GEB 3006) under a 15-hour header, so the term is transcribed at 15 credits. (2) Junior Spring lists 'QMB 3602' with no title; title 'Business Research for Decision Making' taken from the same official site's accounting degree page. (3) Senior Fall includes an explicit 'General Elective (2 credit)' row, transcribed at 2 credits. (4) Term headers sum to 122 (15+15+15+15+15+16+15+16); the UCF degree requirement is a minimum 120 unduplicated semester hours, so the plan as published slightly exceeds the minimum. (5) GEP/ELECT/BUSEL/ECOREL are placeholder codes for student-choice slots (choice:true) per the page's 'Foundation'/'General Elective'/'Business Elective'/'Economics Restricted Elective' rows; all other rows are fixed courses with distinct codes. (6) Business-core and economics courses categorized as 'major' (schema has no 'core' category); GEB career-series courses also 'major'. (7) prereq arrays are left empty: the plan page does not list per-course prerequisites.",
